{
  "reasons": {
    "noExcessiveCognitiveComplexity": "Functions written before the gate (route handlers, parsers of AI session files, page components). Each is split when it is next changed; none may grow.",
    "noExcessiveLinesPerFunction": "Large page components and the session file parsers, written before the gate; split when next changed.",
    "useMaxParams": "Constructors and helpers written before the gate that take their collaborators one by one.",
    "noMisusedPromises": "Biome's nursery rule reads `if (running) return running` (is there a promise already?) as a promise used as a condition; reviewed, not a bug.",
    "duplicate": "Copies found when the gate was added (route boilerplate, similar page sections); merged when next changed, none may be added.",
    "effectRace": "Effects written before the rule that load data for an id (project, tab, server) without an ignore flag; the worst case is a moment of the previous item's data. The ones that could write wrong data or show wrong search results (file content, env history, table rows, searches) were fixed when the rule came in; the rest get the flag when next changed.",
    "serverLeak": "apperrors.ts only holds the timer as text: it is part of the small error SDK Igrek hands to the user's own app, where the page lives as long as the timer."
  },
